  <h1>The Scourge That Paralyzed a Nation: How One Man's Needle Ended Polio</h1>
  <p class="dek">In 1952, polio paralyzed 21,000 Americans in a single summer. Parents stopped letting their children outside. One man with a needle refused to patent the sun. 99.99% of the disease is now gone.</p>
